1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,652
Welcome to Atomic Education.

2
00:00:02,711 --> 00:00:09,852
This lesson was written by the Atomic teaching team to help you learn Cambridge Lower Secondary Science with confidence.

3
00:00:09,852 --> 00:00:10,560
Let's begin!

4
00:00:11,619 --> 00:00:15,455
Welcome to Unit 12: Renewable and Non-Renewable Energy Resources.

5
00:00:16,514 --> 00:00:22,593
Solar panels use photovoltaic cells: particles of light, called photons, knock electrons out of atoms,

6
00:00:22,593 --> 00:00:28,671
making an electric current. It's clean and renewable. But which energy resources are truly sustainable?

7
00:00:29,730 --> 00:00:33,330
An energy resource is anything from which we can get energy.

8
00:00:33,330 --> 00:00:37,166
Wood can be burnt to release its stored chemical energy as heat.

9
00:00:37,166 --> 00:00:42,596
Others include fossil fuels like coal and oil, gases, nuclear fuels like uranium, biofuels,

10
00:00:42,596 --> 00:00:44,484
and electricity stored in cells.

11
00:00:45,543 --> 00:00:48,789
Every part of society needs energy: homes for heating,

12
00:00:48,789 --> 00:00:54,454
lighting and cooking; transport; industry; computers and data centres; farming; and healthcare.

13
00:00:54,454 --> 00:00:57,759
Most of the energy we use is in the form of electricity.

14
00:00:58,818 --> 00:01:04,838
Imagine life without a reliable energy supply: homes go dark, factories stop and the economy suffers.

15
00:01:04,838 --> 00:01:08,792
Today we use more technology, and so more energy, than ever before.

16
00:01:09,851 --> 00:01:15,752
Energy is needed in every part of daily life. Here are four places that depend on a reliable supply.

17
00:01:16,811 --> 00:01:23,126
At home we use energy for cooking, lighting, heating or cooling rooms, and charging our phones and laptops.

18
00:01:24,185 --> 00:01:30,617
Buses, cars, trains and planes all need a fuel, such as petrol or diesel, or electricity stored in batteries.

19
00:01:31,676 --> 00:01:38,168
Hospitals need power all day and night. Many have back-up generators so that life-support machines never stop.

20
00:01:39,227 --> 00:01:43,004
Every message and photo you store on lai sits in a data centre,

21
00:01:43,004 --> 00:01:46,368
where thousands of computers run and are cooled non-stop.

22
00:01:47,427 --> 00:01:53,092
If the energy supply fails, homes go dark, transport stops and hospitals rely on back-up power.

23
00:01:53,092 --> 00:01:56,751
Pause and think: which energy resource does your home rely on?
